<p class="hero-intro">
    Giannis Antetokounmpo stands 6'11" with a 7'4" wingspan and a max vertical reach of 12'2" — roughly 26 inches above the rim. After 13 seasons, two MVPs, a Defensive Player of the Year award, and a 2021 championship in Milwaukee, the Bucks traded him to the Miami Heat this offseason in one of the largest deals of the summer. Here is the full breakdown of the measurements behind the “Greek Freak,” and what his frame means for his new team.
  </p>
</div><div class="article-wrap">
<div class="content">

<h2>The Verified Measurements</h2>
<div class="player-card">
<div class="player-name">Giannis Antetokounmpo</div>
<div class="player-sub">Miami Heat · Forward · Age 31 · Two-Time MVP</div>
<div class="player-stats">
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">6'11"</div>
