</div>
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">7'4"</div>
<div class="player-stat-label">Wingspan — +5" over height</div>
</div>
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">12'2"</div>
<div class="player-stat-label">Max Vertical Reach</div>
</div>
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">~35"</div>
<div class="player-stat-label">Estimated Vertical Jump</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Antetokounmpo was drafted 15th overall by Milwaukee in 2013 at a measured 6-foot-8.5. Bucks staff noticed he was still growing partway through his rookie season, and by year's end he had added roughly two and a half inches, settling at his current listed height of 6'11". His wingspan of approximately 7'4" gives him one of the largest wingspan-to-height differentials of any forward in the league — about five inches of extra length beyond his already elite height.</p>
<p>His max vertical reach of 12 feet 2 inches ties for one of the highest marks ever recorded on DraftExpress' combine database, putting him in company with the tallest, longest leapers the sport has measured. His actual standing vertical jump — the distance between standing reach and peak reach — is commonly cited around 34 to 40 inches, though unlike his height and wingspan, that specific number has never been an official, disclosed combine result. It is an estimate built from reach measurements and game film, not a verified test.</p>

<h2>How His Frame Ranks Among NBA Forwards</h2>
<div class="rank-card">
<div class="rank-title">Antetokounmpo's Physical Profile vs Positional Norms</div>
<div class="rank-row">
<div class="rank-label"><strong>Height</strong>6'11"</div>
